WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.713
Secure Go REST APIs are built from durable
habits.

2
00:00:02.793 --> 00:00:04.637
Treat every route as a security boundary.

3
00:00:04.717 --> 00:00:07.562
Validate request bodies, parameters,
headers, content types,

4
00:00:07.642 --> 00:00:09.381
and identifiers before sensitive use.

5
00:00:09.461 --> 00:00:12.622
Keep handlers small enough that parsing,
validation, authorization,

6
00:00:12.702 --> 00:00:15.600
business logic, and response writing are
visible during review.

7
00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.473
Use middleware intentionally, but do not
hide authorization.

8
00:00:18.553 --> 00:00:20.344
Authentication identifies the caller;

9
00:00:20.424 --> 00:00:24.007
authorization decides whether that caller
may perform the action on the object,

10
00:00:24.087 --> 00:00:25.352
tenant, and workflow state.

11
00:00:25.432 --> 00:00:29.015
Enforce sensitive decisions on the server
and close to the protected operation.

12
00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:30.992
Protect data on the way in and on the way
out.

13
00:00:31.072 --> 00:00:33.653
Use safe database patterns, preserve
tenant separation,

14
00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:37.158
return explicit response models, map
errors to safe responses, redact logs,

15
00:00:37.238 --> 00:00:40.294
and keep secrets out of source, responses,
and operational systems.

16
00:00:40.374 --> 00:00:44.062
Bound request size, time, goroutines,
files, connections, and downstream calls.

17
00:00:44.142 --> 00:00:46.092
Finally, govern the system around the
code.

18
00:00:46.172 --> 00:00:49.333
Review dependencies, validate
configuration, test rejection paths,

19
00:00:49.413 --> 00:00:52.153
use CI checks, document releases, and keep
patch paths clear.

20
00:00:52.233 --> 00:00:55.658
A secure Go REST API is a predictable
boundary between untrusted requests and

21
00:00:55.738 --> 00:00:57.108
trusted business operations.

22
00:00:57.188 --> 00:01:00.824
Its strength comes from the same habits
applied repeatedly across every route and

23
00:01:00.904 --> 00:01:03.380
release, not from a one-time review or
checklist alone.
